//
//  Signing.local.xcconfig.example
//  Sycamore
//
//  Template for a per-developer signing override. To use it:
//
//      cp Config/Signing.local.xcconfig.example Config/Signing.local.xcconfig
//
//  then fill in your team and bundle id below and close/reopen the project (Xcode reads
//  xcconfigs when the project loads). The real file is gitignored — it is yours, it never
//  travels, and nobody else's device build changes because of it.
//
//  Only override what you need. Anything left commented out keeps the default from
//  `Signing.xcconfig`.
//

// Xcode → Settings → Accounts → your Apple ID → the ten-character team id in the team list.
// A free Apple ID's is its "(Personal Team)" entry — free provisioning signs for a real device
// fine; the build just expires after seven days and you re-run from Xcode to refresh it.
// SYCAMORE_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345

// Must be one nobody has registered. `com.cjgimena.app` is taken — it belongs to the team
// above — and a duplicate fails as "Failed to register bundle identifier".
// SYCAMORE_BUNDLE_ID = com.yourname.sycamore

// Uncomment — leaving it empty — if you are signing with a free Apple ID. A Personal Team
// cannot sign Sign In with Apple, and Xcode fails the build rather than dropping the claim.
// Paid memberships should leave this alone: your own App ID can carry the capability once you
// tick it on developer.apple.com.
// SYCAMORE_ENTITLEMENTS =
